  "id": "supportive-expressive-psychotherapy",
  "term": "supportive-expressive psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Supportive-expressive psychotherapy is a form of psychotherapy described as one in which the therapeutic alliance mainly provides a helpful setting that allows the treatment to work. In this approach, the relationship supports the therapy process rather than being treated as the main active ingredient itself.",
